body:
The implementation only clears undo history for the currently assigned animation, but the AnimationPlayer may have multiple animations with undo histories that reference the deleted resource. This means ghost dependencies could persist in non-active animations. Consider iterating through all animations in the player and clearing undo history for each one, or alternatively, clearing the entire undo history for the AnimationPlayer itself.
```suggestion
	EditorUndoRedoManager *undo_redo = EditorUndoRedoManager::get_singleton();

	// Clear undo history for all animations in the player to avoid ghost dependencies
	// in non-active animations that may still reference the deleted resource.
	TypedArray<StringName> anim_names = player->get_animation_list();
	for (int i = 0; i < anim_names.size(); i++) {
		StringName anim_name = anim_names[i];
		Ref<Animation> anim = player->get_animation(anim_name);
		if (anim.is_null()) {
			continue;
		}
		undo_redo->clear_history(undo_redo->get_history_id_for_object(anim.ptr()));
	}
```

